    <title>The Re-Inventors S3 - "The Bourne Submarine"</title>
    <desc>Today we will see if it is possible to make an old-school wooden submarine under water and above all back on the surface.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126093227 +0000" stop="20261126100555 +0000">
    <title>Extremes S1 - "Tall Buildings, Fast Animals and Expensive Cities"</title>
    <desc>In this episode of Extremes, we explore tall buildings, fast animals, expensive cities and extremely impressive basketball records.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126100555 +0000" stop="20261126103923 +0000">
    <title>Extremes S1 - "Long Lives, Destructive Weather and Speed Records"</title>
    <desc>In this episode of Extremes, you will learn about extreme close-up photography, long lives, destructive weather and speed records.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126103923 +0000" stop="20261126111251 +0000">
    <title>Extremes S1 - "Physics, Space and Wealth"</title>
    <desc>In this episode of Extremes, we’ll explore all things extreme in physics, space and wealth plus take a look at the smallest creatures on Earth.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126111251 +0000" stop="20261126114619 +0000">
    <title>Extremes S1 - "Largest Animals, Human Bodies and Football"</title>
    <desc>In this episode of Extremes, we will be exploring the largest animals, extreme facts about the human body and record breaking extremes in football and the field of music.</desc>
  </programme>
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126114619 +0000" stop="20261126124718 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Across Oceans"</title>
    <desc>Throughout history, human society has run on trade. The innovations that allowed faster and more accurate oceanic travel revolutionized the world. New inventions now help people and goods move on the water faster for recreation and commerce.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126124718 +0000" stop="20261126135300 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Across Continents"</title>
    <desc>Never in the history of humanity have so many of us been mobile. New innovations propel us into the world of self-driving cars and high-speed trains.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126135300 +0000" stop="20261126150058 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Into the Skies"</title>
    <desc>Growth in air transportation is set to soar, carrying over 10 billion passengers every year by 2050. To cope requires us to radically rethink aircraft design. Join us as we look into the world's most innovative research and development labs.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126150058 +0000" stop="20261126160827 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Into Space"</title>
    <desc>The most innovative area of human motion lies not on Earth, but with the exploration of space. Meet the private space entrepreneurs jostling to offer the tantalizing prospect of cheap, frequent travel beyond the atmosphere into Earth orbit.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126160827 +0000" stop="20261126162933 +0000">
    <title>Breakthrough S1 - "Coronavirus: Don't Blame Bats"</title>
    <desc>Bats are getting their share of the blame for the COVID-19 pandemic, but are they really at fault?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126162933 +0000" stop="20261126164714 +0000">
    <title>Breakthrough S1 - "Peru's Mysterious Cloud Warriors"</title>
    <desc>Archeologists and geneticists are uncovering surprising details about one of the most mysterious civilizatiions in Pre-Incan South America.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126164714 +0000" stop="20261126170815 +0000">
    <title>Breakthrough S1 - "Decoding Megalodon"</title>
    <desc>Scientists have concluded that "meg" was able to achieve its gargantuan proportions by starting its carnivorous diet early -- in the womb.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126170815 +0000" stop="20261126180558 +0000">
    <title>Singapore's Field Of Dreams</title>
    <desc>Follow the construction of Singapore’s billion-dollar sports hub, featuring a 55,000-seat stadium with a groundbreaking retractable domed roof.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126180558 +0000" stop="20261126191111 +0000">
    <title>Top 10: The Art of Architecture S1 - "Museums and Galleries: Architectural Treasures"</title>
    <desc>Bilbao, Amsterdam, Antwerp and Florence belong to a dynamic group of cities that preserve the heritage of humanity through museums.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126191111 +0000" stop="20261126201619 +0000">
    <title>Top 10: The Art of Architecture S1 - "TV Towers: Complex and Gracious"</title>
    <desc>Television towers are a distinctive type of structure that have long transcended the utilitarian purpose they were designed for.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126201619 +0000" stop="20261126204942 +0000">
    <title>Monkey Thieves S1 - "Skid Row"</title>
    <desc>The drought means the monkey troop are facing starvation, but they are saved in the nick of time when a devout Hindu brings them bagful’s of fruit and treats.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126204942 +0000" stop="20261126212308 +0000">
    <title>Orphans of the Wild S1 - "Operations Wild Dog"</title>
    <desc>Almost fully grown now, the wild dogs are Marlice’s prized project and biggest responsibility - when one gets bitten by a snake, they move quickly to save her.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126212308 +0000" stop="20261126215633 +0000">
    <title>Orphans of the Wild S1 - "Cheetah Rescue"</title>
    <desc>A caracal with a broken leg arrives needing immediate medical attention. When the owner of two tame cheetahs also breaks a leg, Marlice must rescue them as well.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126215633 +0000" stop="20261126222957 +0000">
    <title>Orphans of the Wild S1 - "Tooth Trouble &amp; Game Count"</title>
    <desc>With all the rain came an abundance of animals - to count them Rudie takes to the air, but only after saving a cheetah’s life on the operating table.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126222957 +0000" stop="20261126230320 +0000">
    <title>Orphans of the Wild S1 - "Preparing for the Big Release"</title>
    <desc>In their biggest effort to release animals back into the wild - Marlice and Rudie must dart and capture seven cheetahs and one leopard - all in one day.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126230320 +0000" stop="20261126233628 +0000">
    <title>Orphans of the Wild S1 - "The Big Release"</title>
    <desc>Seven cheetahs and one leopard get their first taste of freedom in an epic release effort - one that Marlice and Rudie have been dreaming about.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261126233628 +0000" stop="20261127000409 +0000">
    <title>Animal Ambulance S1 - "Accidents, Surgeries and Fearful Friends"</title>
    <desc>The team springs into action for a a puppy hit by car, Westie's unusual surgery and a Staffordshire that fears fireworks.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127000409 +0000" stop="20261127003217 +0000">
    <title>Animal Ambulance S1 - "Lumps, Jabs and Tiny Patients"</title>
    <desc>The team treats Labrador Scuby’s lumps, nervous cat Wotzit’s jabs, rescue collie Bob, and tiny rat Squeaky’s stomach growth in a day of unusual cases.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127003217 +0000" stop="20261127010036 +0000">
    <title>Animal Ambulance S1 - "Paws, Gums and Urgent Care"</title>
    <desc>Team faces a day of critical animal care with plus-size cat Bob to Angus’s gum surgery, a Husky’s sore paw, and Bandit’s urgent bladder operation.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127010036 +0000" stop="20261127012831 +0000">
    <title>Animal Ambulance S1 - "Kittens, Puppies and Senior Paws"</title>
    <desc>Debbie cares for abandoned kittens, vets neuter Chihuahua pups,Sonia brings in senior Bichon Mitch, and the mobile clinic checks over playful puppies.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127012831 +0000" stop="20261127015606 +0000">
    <title>Animal Ambulance S1 - "Bladders, Knees and Rescue Tales"</title>
    <desc>The team tackles a dog with bladder issues, a delicate knee operation, diabetes checks for a blind Husky, and urgent care for a stray cat in need.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127015606 +0000" stop="20261127030004 +0000">
    <title>Wild Faces of Switzerland S1 - "The Jura Mountains"</title>
    <desc>The ibex, marmot, and European adder have all developed strategies to survive the alpine winter.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127030004 +0000" stop="20261127040448 +0000">
    <title>Wild Faces of Switzerland S1 - "Ticino"</title>
    <desc>Learn about four different regions of Switzerland. From the rugged mountains of the Ticino High Alps to the lovely Muggio Valley in the southernmost corner of Ticino, hardly any other canton is so full of contrasts.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127040448 +0000" stop="20261127050854 +0000">
    <title>Wild Faces of Switzerland S1 - "Water and Ice"</title>
    <desc>The river called Aare is the only body of water that runs through Switzerland. It rises from a source in the Bernese Alps and finally flows into the Rhine. The Aere offers an important habitat for flora and fauna.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261127050854 +0000" stop="20261127053853 +0000">
    <title>Wild Walk S1 - "Elephants"</title>
    <desc>Can the African elephant evers be tamed? Is it possible to sustain an entire tourism industry based on them being domesticated? Swati walks with the elephants of Knysna park while these questions are asked.</desc>
  </programme>
  
